    <node id="req:WF-008"><data key="label">WF-008</data><data key="ntype">requirement</data><data key="nprops">{"deps": "AI", "location": "BE", "section": "29. Critical workflows (§18) and documentation (§22, §23)", "spec_section": "§18", "status": "TESTED", "text": "AI question workflow"}</data></node>
    <node id="req:WF-009"><data key="label">WF-009</data><data key="ntype">requirement</data><data key="nprops">{"deps": "AUTH-013", "location": "BE", "section": "29. Critical workflows (§18) and documentation (§22, §23)", "spec_section": "§18", "status": "TESTED", "text": "Account deletion workflow"}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/01"><data key="label">Sign-up. The sign-up form posts `POST /auth/register` with email, password, display name, country, currency, time zone, locale, `accept_terms`, …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 1}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/02"><data key="label">Verification. The link opens `/verify-email` with a token, which the page posts to `POST /auth/email/verify`. Tokens are 256-bit, hashed, single use and …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 2}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/03"><data key="label">Sign-in. `POST /auth/login` checks the throttle counters (per email hash and per IP), verifies the password and creates a `user_sessions` row. Web receives …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 3}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/04"><data key="label">Staying signed in. `GET /auth/session` returns the account summary. `POST /auth/refresh` rotates the tokens (empty body for web cookies; `refresh_token` for …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 4}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/05"><data key="label">Password reset. `POST /auth/password/forgot` always answers the same way and emails a 1-hour link (`auth.send_password_reset`). `POST /auth/password/reset` …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 5}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/06"><data key="label">Security settings. `POST /me/password` changes the password and signs out other sessions. Two-step verification: `POST /me/mfa/totp/setup` (returns …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 6}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.1/07"><data key="label">Security-relevant events are written to `security_events` and the person is emailed about important ones (`auth.send_security_email`); an in-app copy goes …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.1", "order": 7}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/01"><data key="label">Each page is uploaded with purpose `receipt` ([2.10](#210-files-and-storage)).</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 1}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/02"><data key="label">`POST /receipts` (with `Idempotency-Key`) takes the page `file_ids` in order and an optional note. By default the receipt is `needs_review` and nothing is …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 2}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/03"><data key="label">`receipts.extract` runs the configured `Extractor` and stores a new `receipt_extractions` version with candidate values, confidences, `receipt_line_items`, …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 3}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/04"><data key="label">`PATCH /receipts/{id}/review` saves the reviewed values (status `reviewed`). `POST /receipts/{id}/process` reads again (a new version).</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 4}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/05"><data key="label">`GET /receipts/{id}/match-candidates` suggests existing transactions with `reason_codes` (`same_amount` or `amount_close`, `same_date` or `near_date`, …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 5}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/06"><data key="label">`POST /receipts/{id}/unlink`, `POST /receipts/{id}/discard` and `POST /receipts/{id}/restore` (optional `?version=`) are audited.</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 6}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.10/07"><data key="label">`GET /receipts` is the inbox, newest first, cursor-paged, filtered by status.</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.10", "order": 7}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/01"><data key="label">Upload the file with purpose `statement_import`, then `POST /imports` (with `Idempotency-Key`) naming the account. The batch is `uploaded`; `imports.parse` …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 1}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/02"><data key="label">The parser suggests a mapping with `mapping_note_codes` (`no_header_row`, `ambiguous_date_order`, `decimal_comma`, `check_sign_convention`, ...). When the …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 2}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/03"><data key="label">Normalization computes fingerprints and flags duplicates: `already_imported` (same fingerprint or external ID) and `possible_duplicate` with reason codes. …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 3}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/04"><data key="label">`GET /imports/{id}/rows` lists rows by status; `PATCH /imports/{id}/rows/{rowId}` corrects a value (`posted_date`, `amount`, `category_id`, `description`) …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 4}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/05"><data key="label">`POST /imports/{id}/confirm` (with `Idempotency-Key`) queues `imports.process`, which creates one transaction per row in its own database transaction with …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 5}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/06"><data key="label">Matching. `GET /reconciliation/candidates` returns suggestions of kind `statement_to_ledger`, `pending_to_posted` or `manual_to_imported`, one-to-one or …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 6}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.11/07"><data key="label">Balance check. `POST /accounts/{id}/reconciliations` compares the ledger with a statement balance (or amount owed for a card) on a date and records …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.11", "order": 7}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.12/01"><data key="label">Analytics are computed on read from the person's own records: | Endpoint | Returns | |---|---| | `GET /analytics/cash-flow` | Income, gross expense, …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.12", "order": 1}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.12/02"><data key="label">Reports. `POST /reports` with `report_type` (`monthly_summary`, `yearly_summary`, `income`, `expense`, `cash_flow`, `category`, `merchant`, `account`, …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.12", "order": 2}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.12/03"><data key="label">`GET /reports` and `GET /reports/{id}` show status; `GET /reports/{id}/download` returns a short-lived signed link while the report has not expired (7 days …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.12", "order": 3}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.12/04"><data key="label">Schedules. `POST /reports/schedules` (weekly or monthly), `GET /reports/schedules`, `GET /reports/schedules/{id}`, `PATCH /reports/schedules/{id}` (with …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.12", "order": 4}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.12/05"><data key="label">Other exports: group expenses (`GET /groups/{id}/export`, CSV), a goal's contributions (`GET /goals/{id}/export`, CSV) and the full data export …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.12", "order": 5}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.13/01"><data key="label">AI is off unless the owner sets `AI_PROVIDER=anthropic` and `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. The default is `disabled`.</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.13", "order": 1}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.13/02"><data key="label">Even then, a person must grant the `ai_processing` consent (`POST /me/consents`) and turn AI on with `PATCH /ai/preferences`; without the consent the answer …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.13", "order": 2}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.13/03"><data key="label">With the provider off, consent missing, AI turned off or the daily cap reached, `POST /ai/ask` and `POST /ai/report-summary` answer deterministically …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.13", "order": 3}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.13/04"><data key="label">When on, the model gets minimal, redacted context and only read-only tools that run as the caller under RLS. Untrusted text is fenced, outputs are …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.13", "order": 4}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.14/01"><data key="label">Daily, `insights.generate_all` queues `insights.generate` per person; `POST /ai/insights/generate` runs it on demand. Despite the `/ai` prefix, this …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.14", "order": 1}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.14/02"><data key="label">Each of the 11 rules (`backend/internal/insights/insights.go` and `more_rules.go`) produces candidates with evidence, a confidence and a fingerprint. Rules …</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.14", "order": 2}</data></node>
    <node id="step:feature-3.14/03"><data key="label">Up to three new `notice` or `warning` insights per run create an `insight` notification ("Something unusual in your spending"), linking to `/insights/{id}`.</data><data key="ntype">step</data><data key="nprops">{"flow": "flow:feature-3.14", "order": 3}</data></node>
